# mgcabin.msg - the cabinet beside Moriarty's terminal (mgcabin.ssl). One entry per line; no braces in comments.

# 100 to 102: look (locked, unlocked) and examine.
{100}{}{You see a dented metal cabinet with a padlock through the hasp.}
{101}{}{You see a dented metal cabinet. The padlock hangs open.}
{102}{}{Somebody has scratched C.M. into the paint, in case of doubt, and then underlined it.}

# 120 to 123: the padlock picked, or not.
{120}{}{The padlock drops open.}
{121}{}{The padlock holds. It is small, cheap, and at the moment smarter than you.}
{122}{}{Your pick bends. The padlock does not. You straighten the pick and your pride as best you can.}
{123}{}{It is not locked.}

# 130, 131: the card inside the door.
{130}{}{Taped inside the door is a card with a single word on it, in a tidy, grasping hand. It can only be the password to Moriarty's terminal. You commit it to memory.}
{131}{}{Taped inside the door is a card with one word on it: the password to Moriarty's terminal. You know it already.}

{140}{}{Moriarty's key is far too big for the padlock.}
{141}{}{You find no traps, only a padlock.}
